Description: Standalone local voice input and speech-to-text
 Sasayaki records audio, transcribes it locally with an offline
 SenseVoice engine, and pastes the result into the focused application.
 It is a single standalone binary, independent of any desktop environment;
 when the Sumika Shell desktop is present it additionally registers as a
 first-class module.
 .
 The private Python runtime, speech model, and systemd user service are
 provisioned per-user by `sasayaki setup`, so they are not package
 dependencies.
